<title>USA: Boeing says delivered 62 airplanes in Q4.</title>
<headline>Boeing says delivered 62 airplanes in Q4.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Boeing Co on Monday said it delivered 62 commercial jet transport airplanes in the fourth quarter, bringing the total number of deliveries in 1996 to 218.</p>
<p>The fourth quarter deliveries consisted of 23 737 models, 10 747s, 8 757s, 13 767s and 8 777s, Boeing said in a statement.</p>
<p>The 218 deliveries for the year consisted of 76 737s, 26 747s, 42 757s, 42 767s and 32 777s.</p>
</text>
